The attached image, Figure 5 from the PDF, illustrates how Nano-11 enhances the uptake of adsorbed antigens by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs). Panel A, a flow cytometry dot plot, shows that while soluble FITC-labeled ovalbumin (OVA) alone is taken up modestly, and AF647-labeled Nano-11 is also taken up, there is a significant increase in the uptake of both Nano-11 and OVA by BMDCs when OVA is adsorbed to Nano-11 (Nano-11+OVA). Panel B, a histogram of FITC-OVA fluorescence, further confirms this by showing a marked shift to higher fluorescence intensity for cells treated with Nano-11+OVA compared to OVA alone, indicating a greatly increased amount of antigen inside the dendritic cells. This demonstrates Nano-11's role in facilitating antigen delivery to APCs.